diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6d352dc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Chat bots
+
+Bots are STI `User` identities with an owning user and a unique `bot_code`. This
+lets bots participate in existing room memberships and message authorship, so
+message broadcasts, unread updates, and push notifications use the normal chat
+flow. Creating a bot uses the regular new-user callback to grant it access to
+all open rooms; closed-room membership can be managed through the existing
+room member settings.
+
+`POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_code/messages` authenticates by the bot code and
+uses the unparsed request body as the message body. It accepts no attachment or
+JSON envelope. A bot may post only to rooms where it has membership. Codes are
+shown in the owner/admin bot list and are not included in other user-facing
+views.
+
+Successful requests respond with `201 Created` and a message resource `Location`.
+Empty request bodies return `422`, invalid room IDs return `404`, and invalid
+or inactive bot codes return `401`.
